{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration/recovery policy in specifications. The policy gives one controllable action per active decision/recovery state, keeps all uncontrollable events defined in every state, treats obstacle events as safety-critical preemptions in action states, prefers forward progress in clear space, uses directed turns for ordinary recovery, uses move_backward only in dedicated front-obstacle recovery, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort stuck state after repeated front blockage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensor outcomes from motion capabilities in G so E can impose safe exploration logic cleanly.",
    "Use one main policy specification plus a small last-resort escalation specification to keep helper states few while enforcing conservative-but-progress-seeking recovery."
  ],
